Source: pve-meta
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Julius Arkenberg <julius@rkenberg.de>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               libperl-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/arki05/pve-meta

Package: pve-meta
Architecture: any
Depends: pve-manager (>= 9.0),
         libpve-meta-rs-perl (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Structured, versioned metadata store for Proxmox VE
 pve-meta adds a structured (YAML/TOML/JSON) metadata document per guest and
 for the datacenter, stored under /etc/pve/meta and replicated by pmxcfs like
 any other cluster file. The API is served natively by pveproxy/pvedaemon
 (PVE::API2::Meta, see docs/NATIVE-API-SPEC.md) under /api2/json/meta/...; this
 package also ships the pve-meta CLI (runs the same handlers in-process
 against the store, no daemon needed), the wasm editor UI, and the web UI /
 guest-lifecycle integration patches. The standalone HTTPS daemon
 alternative (pve-metad, port 8007) is a separate, optional package.

Package: libpve-meta-rs-perl
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, ${perl:Depends}
Description: pve-meta guest lifecycle hooks for PVE (Rust, perlmod)
 PVE::RS::Meta, a Perl binding (via perlmod) to pve-meta's guest metadata
 store, exposing snapshot/rollback/delsnap/clone/destroy lifecycle hooks and
 vzdump backup/restore export/import for use from PVE's own Perl code
 (pve-container, qemu-server, pve-guest-common). Also used by
 PVE::API2::Meta (package pve-meta) to serve the pve-meta API natively.

Package: pve-metad
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: pve-meta HTTPS API daemon (standalone, optional)
 pve-metad serves the pve-meta API on its own HTTPS port (8007), as a
 standalone alternative to the native pveproxy/pvedaemon integration
 provided by the pve-meta package (see docs/NATIVE-API-SPEC.md). Not
 installed or required by default, and not depended on by pve-meta.
